      "tools": [
        {
          "name": "ff14_market_query",
          "capability_id": "ff14.market.query",
          "parameter_mapping": {
            "query": "query",
            "server": "server",
            "dc": "dc",
            "region": "region",
            "quality": "quality",
            "intent": "intent"
          },
          "description": "Query public FF14 per-item Gil prices by an item name or ID explicitly present in the current user message. Scope: server/dc/region; quality: all/nq/hq; intent: overview/min/listings. On ambiguity show candidate names and ask for one unique full name (or full name + \u90a3\u4e2a). Never guess or query a pending candidate to bypass selection; use select to preserve context. Ordinal choices are unsupported. For lowest price / where cheapest (including Chinese equivalents), prefer intent=min; overview is for general market metrics. After success or usable partial facts suffice, answer directly; do not query extra servers without a new explicit user scope. Place Universalis source, fetched/cache age, price source age and limited coverage/non-realtime caveat next to prices. Use verified world_name only; unknown stays unknown. Do not infer HQ uses, restocking or purchase advice. On errors explain briefly and await user clarification; never change query parameters to bypass confirmation."
        },
        {
          "name": "ff14_market_select",
          "capability_id": "ff14.market.select",
          "parameter_mapping": {
            "batch_id": "batch_id",
            "generation": "generation",
            "item_id": "item_id"
          },
          "description": "Continue the current user's pending FF14 query only after a new user message confirms a unique full candidate name: name, name + \u90a3\u4e2a, \u9009/\u9009\u62e9/\u5c31/\u5c31\u9009 + name; or \u9009\u62e9\u7269\u54c1 <ID>. Use prior batch_id/generation and the matching item_id. The module validates the real event, not model assertions. Questions, negations, multiple names, duplicate names and ordinal choices require clarification. Preserve original scope, quality, intent and configuration revisions. After success or usable partial facts suffice, answer directly with source and limited coverage/non-realtime caveat adjacent to prices; do not issue extra server queries without a new user instruction. Unknown world names remain unknown; do not infer HQ uses or restocking advice."
        }
      ],
